{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = Gotoran Lament|2 = The Farmer enters Olivia's house and finds her in the cellar drinking wine and listening to a music recording. She says its by Haruhi Kiyoko, a famous Gotoran violinist. When the war started, radio broadcasts were stopped and now this recording is the only way Olivia can hear her music. She worries about Haruhi's safety and tells the Farmer her parents are immigrants from Gotoro. Like Haruhi, Olivia does not know the fate of her friends and family in the Gotoro Empire. Feeling emotional, she shares a glass of Ring Fruit wine from the Fern Islands with the Farmer. Olivia mentions that Suki, the traveling merchant, sells smuggled Gotoran goods and wonders about the family that must have owned a porcelain dish she purchased from Suki. Olivia and the Farmer continue to drink until Olivia asks to be alone. The dark conversation has left too much on her mind. She thanks the Farmer for visiting and turns her music back on. Alone again, Olivia says to herself "Edward... I miss you."<sup>(+50 friendship)</sup>}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

