{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = A Full House|2 = Upon entering the saloon, the Farmer finds almost all of the town there, including people not normally there, like the Wizard, Marlon, Haley, and Caroline. Speech bubbles appear over many of their heads as they all talk. Olivia calls the Farmer over and says she's never seen the saloon this packed. She says she'll catch Emily's attention for an order as soon as the busy barkeep can see them. Olivia tells the Farmer that the wine she's drinking is from Sunshine Vineyard, a vintner all the way out in the Fern Islands. She shares that she doesn't like beer and prefers dry red wines instead. She comments that the Farmer must live a demanding life and asks how they do it. In mild shock the Farmer sometimes survives on forage and on-the-go cooking, she offers a home-cooked meal in the future. Emily apologizes for the delay and says she's had her hands full tonight, then asks the Farmer what they'd like to drink. The Farmer is able to choose between five drinks with different comments from Emily for each. Olivia then says that Emily is a wonderful waitress and her own favorite cocktail is the Red Moon. Emily returns with the Farmer's drink and Olivia tells the Farmer she wants to share stories about her family in the Gotoro Empire as the camera fades out.<sup>(+50 friendship)</sup>}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

