{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = Baggage of the Heart|2 = Olivia assumes the Farmer has come in regard to her letter, and apologizes if it caused any concern. She wanted to speak in private. Olivia confesses she has not dated since the death of her husband Edward. She is conflicted about dating the Farmer, feeling like she might be betraying Edward. The Farmer can respond:
* '''"You need to follow your heart."'''<sup>(+50 friendship)</sup>
Olivia agrees and says Edward would want her to be happy, not to suffer alone. She admits it's time to move forward. Olivia then invite the Farmer to see more of the art she's been painting.
* '''"You're right. We should call this off."'''<sup>(-750 friendship)</sup>
Olivia slowly agrees and suggests they end the relationship before getting too invested. She says there is too much weighing her down to include someone else in her life romantically, and asks the Farmer to leave. Speaking to her after, Olivia gives the Farmer a Wilted Bouquet and tells them to give it to her to end the relationship.}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

