<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="❇ Show ❇" data-collapsetext="✖ Hide ✖">Marriage <div class=mw-collapsible-toggle-placeholder></div>
<div class="mw-collapsible-content">
{{QuotesTableStart|label = Events}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Spring 8, Morning|quote= "Have you ever encountered any wild animals here in the valley, sweetie? I'm terrified of bears. I hope I never meet one."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Spring 12, Morning|quote= "I'm feeling lazy today. I'm tempted to just stay inside and read. I do miss our library sometimes. I could pick any shelf and find a fascinating story to disappear into for hours."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Spring 15, Evening|quote= "Let's invite Victor over for dinner soon. I don't want him to feel like I'm leaving him behind by joining our family with yours. He should feel welcome here, too."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Spring 23, Evening|quote= "In the city... everything moved so fast. I was always on my way somewhere, never pausing to pay attention to the world around me. It feels nice to slow down and enjoy life with you, [Farmer]."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Summer 5, Morning|quote= "I need to go into the city and pick up some painting supplies soon. I special order most of my supplies, but I still like to look around locally to see if anything unique pops up."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Summer 8, Evening|quote= "Have you ever met the wizard who lives south of town? You're braver than I am. I admire your ability to befriend even the strangest people."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Summer 15, Evening|quote= "The air on the farm smells so clean. If Victor comes over, we should have a picnic outside. He could use some fresh air."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Summer 26, Evening|quote= "Andy made me feel uncomfortable at the saloon tonight. He was staring at me constantly... I heard he's horrible at paying his tab. That's not too surprising."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Fall 1, Morning|quote= "I want to paint the leaves changing in Cindersap Forest. That way, we can remember how the autumn looks all year long. It's a great opportunity to learn how to use colors with more nuance. And what a lovely painting it would be, if done well!"}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Fall 2, Morning|quote= "Fall is such a wonderful season for foraging in the valley. Even the most expensive imported mushrooms can't beat what you can find in the wild here. You should pick some mushrooms for our dinner tonight, sweetie."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Fall 22, Morning|quote= "Caroline purchased an astonishing pair of shoes. She's showing Jodi and I at the town square this afternoon. Oh, that reminds me. I'm running errands today, dear." }}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Fall 23, Evening|quote= "My, my. Quite the chilly day. Perhaps we could settle on the couch with a nice cup of hot chocolate? There's a lovely mix from Grampleton in the cupboard."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Winter 9, Evening|quote= "I ran into Sophia today, such a precious doll."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Winter 15, Morning|quote= "My, it's chilly today, isn't it? I'd like to go paint somewhere scenic."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Winter 19, Evening|quote= "Victor dropped off a book for you, sweetie. He said he thinks you'll enjoy it - it's a memoir from the early days of the Adventurer's Guild. I'm glad you two are getting along."}}
{{QuotesTableRow|title= Winter 26, Morning|quote= "Perhaps I'll make us some mulled cider tonight. Does that sound good, dear? Oh, you're heading out? Have a productive day, sweetie."}}
